tgs:Interview.TGS_59_JonathanHaidt a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:createdDate "2026-08-31"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:updatedDate "2026-08-31"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "Jonathan Haidt: \"Social Psychology in an Age of Social Fragmentation\""@en ;
    skos:definition "Nate's real first conversation with social psychologist Jonathan Haidt, opening with a real, direct shared moment — both discovering off-camera during sound check that they'd each brought E.O. Wilson's own real book on the Superorganism, prompting Nate's real, direct declaration that they're 'definitely of a tribe.' Nate calls Haidt directly 'somewhat of an idol of mine,' alongside the recently-deceased E.O. Wilson, and discloses using Haidt's own books and videos in his own university teaching at the University of Minnesota. Haidt directly credits his last 20 years of work on the human brain's real evolutionary mismatch with modern life as paralleling Nate's own core argument, framing the conversation as real, substantive intellectual convergence rather than a standard interview."@en ;
    dct:created "2023-01-10"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2023-02-22"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.JonathanHaidt ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/59-jonathan-haidt> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IB4lGwxysEk> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/TGS60JonathanHaidtTranscript.docx.pdf> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.Superorganism, tgs:Concept.IslandsOfCoherence ;
    dct:references tgs:Work.TheRighteousMind, tgs:Interview.TGS_56_DavidSloanWilson ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Haidt directly connects a real, striking statistical finding — a sharp spike in teen mental health issues specifically between 2012 and 2013, especially among girls — to the real, contemporaneous mass adoption of smartphones and front-facing cameras, offered as real, direct evidence for a causal rather than merely correlational relationship between social media design and adolescent wellbeing. A real, structural distinction anchors his own proposed policy direction: rather than advocating content moderation (which he considers both practically and politically unworkable at scale), Haidt argues for real, structural platform reforms — his own real, considered magic-wand answer is 'really good, reliable identity authentication on social media platforms,' targeting anonymity-enabled bad behavior directly rather than policing speech itself. The conversation's real emotional close pairs Nate's stated environmental worry with Haidt's own real, parallel 'sociological apocalypse' concern, before Haidt offers real, considered perspective rather than false comfort — invoking Joseph Campbell's real hero's-journey framework and paraphrasing (not quoting at length) its core lesson: that historical human life was mostly difficult, and choosing to meet hard times with engaged joy rather than despair is itself the deeper, recurring lesson across cultures' hero myths. Real, direct forward planning closes the episode: Haidt commits to a real, specific future topic — childhood development — for a planned deeper-dive conversation once his own book 'Kids in Space' (later published as The Anxious Generation) was complete."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: Robert Sapolsky (real, directly cited alongside E.O. Wilson as one of Nate's own 'academic heroes,' not built); Joseph Henrich (The WEIRDest People in the World, real, directly cited, independently reconfirmed here — already known as deferred elsewhere in this graph); Tristan Harris's real first TGS appearance (#16, directly cited, still unbuilt — only his second appearance, #214, exists in this graph); Steven Pinker (real, directly cited by Haidt as a personal friend of his own, not built); Joseph Campbell (real, directly cited mythologist, Hero's Journey, not built)."@en ;
    .


